INT. DECOMMISSIONED SUBMARINE BAY - SPACE STATION - NIGHT CYCLE

A long dim hangar. Hull plates ticking as they cool. A flickering amber strip light. A rack of pressure suits like hanging skins.

CAPTAIN LUCIANA MBEKI-ROSSI, 50s, shaved head, grease-stained flight suit, kneels beside a dark console. Next to her, ENGINEER DORIAN WESTBROOK-ANAND, 30s, arms crossed, watches a diagnostic wheel spin. Further off, MEDIC IMANI SOLBERG, 20s, hugs a first-aid case, her hands trembling. At the hatch, SECURITY CHIEF PAVEL ORLOV-DIALLO, 40s, holds a pulse rifle, eyes on the ceiling. Two more figures stand in shadow by the far bulkhead: LINGUIST ESPERANZA BALOGUN, 30s, in a pale coat, and a young cadet, TEO ABERNATHY-LIU, 19, clutching a datapad.

LUCIANA
Status.

DORIAN
Core's alive. Everything else is asleep.

LUCIANA
Wake it.

DORIAN
I'm trying.

IMANI
(small)
Captain?

LUCIANA
Not now.

IMANI
The hull is making a noise.

Silence. The strip light flickers. A distant, rhythmic tapping rolls through the metal. Pavel's rifle lifts.

PAVEL
It's not the cooling.

ESPERANZA
It's a pattern.

LUCIANA
What kind of pattern?

ESPERANZA
(listening)
Three. Pause. Three.

TEO
Is that Morse?

ESPERANZA
It's a countdown.

COMMS (V.O.)
(crackling, over the intercom)
...bay four... can anyone hear... bay four...

Luciana grabs the handset from the console.

LUCIANA
This is Mbeki-Rossi. Say again.

COMMS (V.O.)
Captain? Thank god. We're locked in the sub bay. The door sealed itself.

LUCIANA
Who is this?

COMMS (V.O.)
Station Operations. We've been tapping on the hull for an hour.

Pavel lowers the rifle slowly. Dorian stands. Imani lets out a breath. The tapping continues, closer now.

LUCIANA
(into the handset)
We're in bay four.

COMMS (V.O.)
No, ma'am. You're not.

Luciana stares at the handset. At the others. At the ceiling, where something taps once, twice, thrice.

DORIAN
(whispering)
If they're locked in the sub bay...

PAVEL
Then what is that?

The tapping stops. A long silence. The strip light dies. In the dark, a soft voice laughs, thin and delighted, from the vent above.

Teo drops the datapad. It clatters. No one picks it up.
